    "summary": "Understand the architectural differences, best use cases, and code patterns for LlamaIndex, LangChain, and LangGraph.",
    "content": "### 1. Lesson Title & Objective\n**Objective:** Understand the core differences, control-flow mechanics, and best use cases for LlamaIndex, LangChain, and LangGraph.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Core Concepts Explained in Simple Words\n\n* **The 3 Personas Analogy:**\n  1. **LlamaIndex = The Master Librarian (Data-Centric):**\n     * **Specialty:** Reading files, splitting chunks, creating indexes, and retrieving documents.\n     * **Best for:** RAG applications, company search engines, and complex PDF search.\n  2. **LangChain (LCEL) = The Swiss Army Knife (Chain-Centric):**\n     * **Specialty:** Linking tools, prompts, and models in a straight forward line using pipes (`|`).\n     * **Best for:** Fast prototypes and simple linear pipelines ($A \to B \to C$).\n  3. **LangGraph = The Factory Automation Machine (Agent-Centric):**\n     * **Specialty:** Running loops, saving state to databases, and building autonomous agents that can fix their own mistakes.\n     * **Best for:** Complex agents, self-correction loops, and human-in-the-loop approvals.\n* **DAGs vs. Cyclic State Machines:**\n  * **DAG (Directed Acyclic Graph):** Moves strictly forward in one direction. Cannot go backwards or loop. (LangChain LCEL).\n  * **Cyclic State Machine:** Can loop backwards ($A \to B \to A$) to retry, test code, or ask for clarification. (LangGraph).\n\n---\n\n### 3. Step-by-Step Architecture & Flow\n\n```text\nDAG (LangChain LCEL) vs. CYCLIC GRAPH (LangGraph)\nLangChain LCEL (Strictly One-Way):\n[ Start ] \u2500\u2500\u25ba [ Step 1: Prompt ] \u2500\u2500\u25ba [ Step 2: LLM ] \u2500\u2500\u25ba [ Step 3: Parser ] \u2500\u2500\u25ba [ End ]\n\nLangGraph (Cyclic State Machine with Loops):\n           \u250c\u2500\u2500\u25ba [ Draft Code ] \u2500\u2500\u25ba [ Run Unit Tests ] \u2500\u2500\u2510\n           \u2502                             \u2502 (Fails)      \u2502 (Passes)\n           \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500 [ Self-Correction Loop ] \u2518              \u25bc\n                                                     [ End ]\n```\n\n---\n\n### 4. Concrete Code Example\n\nHere is how all 3 frameworks handle their primary job:\n\n```python\n# 1. LlamaIndex: Data-first RAG in 3 lines\n# from llama_index.core import VectorStoreIndex, SimpleDirectoryReader\n# docs = SimpleDirectoryReader(\"data\").load_data()\n# query_engine = VectorStoreIndex.from_documents(docs).as_query_engine()\n\n# 2. LangChain: Straightforward LCEL Pipe\nfrom langchain_core.prompts import ChatPromptTemplate\nfrom langchain_core.output_parsers import StrOutputParser\n# chain = prompt | model | StrOutputParser()\n\n# 3. LangGraph: Cyclic graph with loops and memory\nfrom langgraph.graph import StateGraph, START, END\n# builder = StateGraph(State)\n# builder.add_conditional_edges(\"check_test\", router_fn, {\"pass\": END, \"fail\": \"draft_code\"})\n```\n\n---\n\n### 5. 1-Minute Exam Review\n\n* **LlamaIndex:** Data-first framework optimized for search, parsing, and RAG.\n* **LangChain (LCEL):** Code-first framework for linear pipelines using the `|` pipe operator.\n* **LangGraph:** Graph-based runtime built specifically for cycles, loops, state reducers, and agents.\n* **DAG vs. Cycle:** LCEL is strictly a DAG (no loops); LangGraph is cyclic (allows loops and self-correction)."
